      ⎕FC←''

      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs28 #73, 2026-08-11): an
      ⍝ out-of-range indexed assignment to ⎕FC was silently ignored
      ⍝ instead of raising INDEX ERROR -- even though a *reference* to
      ⍝ the same out-of-range index (e.g. ⎕FC[7]) already correctly
      ⍝ raises INDEX ERROR; an assignment must be at least as strict.
      ⍝
      ⎕FC[7]←'x'
INDEX ERROR
      ⎕FC[7]←'x'
      ^     ^
      )MORE
NO )MORE ERROR INFO
      )SIC

